<task id="021" project="spaarkeai-compose-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Opaque-atom node in the TipTap/ProseMirror schema (FR-02, client half)</title>
    <phase>2 Frontend capture</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New client node type in the editor schema (`.ts`/`.tsx`, tags include frontend); a mis-modeled atom drops fields/SDTs on save. FULL per root §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-scoped single node-type addition against a documented projection contract; default sonnet tier is sufficient.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>012</deps>
    <tags>frontend,fluent-ui,docx</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
    <assigned>unassigned</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add a NEW non-editable ProseMirror/TipTap node type that renders the server's opaque atom blocks
    (SDT/content controls, fields, complex/floating objects — the projection side is task 012) as visible,
    non-inline-editable placeholders. Each atom node MUST carry its `w14:paraId` and preserve document order
    relative to the surrounding editable paragraphs (design §5, "Ingest (backend)" → opaque atom blocks;
    §5.0 opaque atoms). The node is an `atom: true`, non-editable leaf: the user can select/move-past it but
    cannot type into it (the step interceptor, task 020, refuses edits routed into it). New node file under
    `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/`; wire it into the ComposeEditor schema.
    MIT ProseMirror base only — NO `@tiptap-pro/*`, no AGPL (NFR-03). Display-only placeholder: the atom's
    OOXML is never opened, so it survives save byte-for-byte on the server side (FR-02 acceptance).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript editor engineer fluent in the ProseMirror/TipTap node schema (atom nodes,
    `NodeView`, node attributes, non-editable leaves). Understands FR-02 (opaque atoms are shown, never
    opened) and invariant I-1/I-4 (the OOXML is authoritative; untouched subtrees stay byte-identical).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A registered TipTap/ProseMirror node type such that a document containing fields/SDT/complex objects
    renders those constructs as placeholder atom nodes: visible, non-editable, each carrying its `paraId`,
    in correct document order among the editable paragraphs. Typing inside an atom is a no-op. The node
    round-trips the projection's atom descriptor (task 012) faithfully so document order + patchability
    survive; the server never opens the atom's bytes.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 "Ingest (backend)" specifies non-renderable constructs become opaque atom blocks — visible,
      non-inline-editable, carrying their paraId so document order + patchability survive. §5.0 names opaque
      atoms as one of the three hard bridge pieces. The projection (server) half is task 012 (FR-02) — it
      emits the atom descriptors this node renders; this task is the client half. The interceptor (task 020)
      refuses edits routed into an atom, so together they make atoms non-editable and order-preserving. This
      is genuinely NEW surface (no existing overlap per spec §New Components).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/opaqueAtomNode.ts — NEW TipTap/ProseMirror atom node type (non-editable leaf carrying `paraId`, rendered as a placeholder NodeView)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx — register the atom node in the editor schema/extension list</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ — task 012 opaque-atom projection descriptors (the shape this node renders); align the atom descriptor contract</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/paraIdExtension.ts — the `w14:paraId` attr convention to mirror on the atom node</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5 (Ingest → opaque atom blocks), §5.0 (opaque atoms)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-02, NFR-03</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">Opaque atoms — server projection (FR-02). Emits the atom descriptors (paraId + kind + order) this node type renders. The descriptor contract MUST be agreed before the client node is finalized.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-02">Non-renderable constructs (SDT/content controls, fields, complex/floating objects) MUST render as non-editable placeholder atom nodes carrying their paraId, preserving document order. Atoms are NEVER opened; they survive save byte-for-byte. Scope: this node type + its registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / I-1, I-4">The atom's OOXML is authoritative and untouched — the client node is display-only; it MUST NOT author or mutate the atom's bytes. Scope: the NodeView (render-only, no editable content hole).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / NFR-03">MIT ProseMirror base + `@tiptap/extension-*` only. MUST NOT add `@tiptap-pro/*`, AGPL, or commercial packages; no EigenPal runtime dependency. Scope: this task's imports/package.json.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">This task adds no fetch (render-only). If any is added it MUST use `@spaarke/auth`; flagged so no ad-hoc token handling is introduced. Scope: the node/NodeView.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Behavior covered by colocated Vitest (full suite in task 024). NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests. Scope: tests under `src/`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ProseMirror atom nodes + NodeView; non-editable leaves; node attributes; TipTap schema registration; projection atom descriptors; client licensing discipline</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="paraId node attr convention" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/paraIdExtension.ts">
        How `w14:paraId` is carried as a hidden node attr — mirror the attr shape on the atom node so its paraId is addressable by the patch model.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Non-editable atom leaf" location="notes/bridge-prior-art.md §3">
        Opaque/non-renderable OOXML constructs render as placeholders holding their paraId so order + patchability survive; the editor never opens them (FR-02).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <justification>
    <existing>None — verified by grep against `Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/`: no node type renders SDT/fields/complex objects. Today such constructs either break the mammoth/projection mount or are dropped (spec §New Components lists the opaque-atom node as the one genuinely-new client surface).</existing>
    <extension>No existing node type can be extended: `paraIdExtension` only tags `paragraph`/`heading` editable nodes; there is no non-editable-leaf node to build on. An atom node is a distinct ProseMirror node kind (`atom: true`), not a variant of an editable node.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, documents containing fields/content controls either error on load or silently drop those constructs on save — the FR-02 acceptance "corpus docs containing fields/SDTs load without editor error; the constructs survive save byte-for-byte" fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (root §8). Load the knowledge files + the task-012 atom descriptor contract. Confirm task 012 is complete (the descriptor shape is agreed). Note this is a display-only client node — no fetch, no save wiring.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Define the atom node">Implement `opaqueAtomNode.ts`: a TipTap/ProseMirror node with `atom: true`, non-editable, `selectable` but not typeable; attrs include `paraId` (mirroring `paraIdExtension`) + the atom `kind`. `parseHTML`/`renderHTML` (or `addAttributes`) round-trip the task-012 descriptor.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Placeholder NodeView">Render a visible, non-editable placeholder NodeView (Fluent v9, theme-token styled) that labels the atom kind and holds no editable content hole. Document order relative to surrounding paragraphs is preserved by node position.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Register in editor">Register the node in `ComposeEditor.tsx`'s schema/extension list so projected atoms mount as this node. Confirm the task-020 interceptor refuses edits routed into it (coordinate the guard). Checkpoint (context-handoff) per root §5.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Local tests + build">Add colocated Vitest tests: atom renders non-editable, carries its paraId, preserves order; typing is a no-op. Run `npm run build:prod` (NOT `npm run build`) for the shared lib; confirm no `@tiptap-pro/*` in the tree.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Close-out">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Fields/SDT render as placeholders in order">
      <steps>Load a projected doc that contains a field and an SDT between two editable paragraphs.</steps>
      <expected>Each construct renders as a visible placeholder atom labeled with its kind, in the correct position between the paragraphs; no editor error on load.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Typing inside an atom is a no-op">
      <steps>Select an atom placeholder and attempt to type / paste into it.</steps>
      <expected>No text is inserted; the atom content is unchanged (non-editable leaf); the caret does not enter the atom.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Atom carries its paraId">
      <steps>Inspect the mounted atom node's attributes after load.</steps>
      <expected>The node's `paraId` attr equals the descriptor's paraId, making it addressable by the patch model.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Render the editor with atom placeholders under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider.</steps>
      <expected>Placeholder chrome (border, label, icon) uses theme tokens and is legible in dark mode; no hard-coded light colors.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the task-012 atom descriptor cannot express a construct the client must render in order (e.g. a nested/floating object with no stable paraId), STOP and surface it (root §6 / §6.5) rather than inventing a client-side identity — the atom's addressability depends on the server descriptor.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/opaqueAtomNode.ts (new non-editable atom node type)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (atom node registered)</output>
    <output type="test">Colocated Vitest tests for atom render/non-editable/order/paraId (extended in task 024)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A doc with fields/SDT renders those constructs as placeholder atom nodes, in correct document order, without editor error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each atom node is non-editable and carries its `paraId` attribute.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Attempting to type inside an atom is a no-op — content unchanged (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `@tiptap-pro/*` / AGPL / EigenPal runtime dependency is introduced; `npm run build:prod` for the shared lib is green (NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The dark-mode render (ADR-021) is legible with theme tokens.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Client half of FR-02; the server projection half is task 012 (agree the atom descriptor contract with it).
    Render-only — no fetch, no save wiring. Client task (no BFF surface) — no publish-size / CVE gate. The
    interceptor (task 020) enforces non-editability at the step level; this task enforces it at the schema
    level (`atom: true`).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
